0,Languages of Tanzania - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Languages_of_Tanzania,"February 9, 2026 - Most languages spoken locally belong to two broad language families: Niger-Congo (Bantu branch) and Nilo-Saharan (Nilotic branch), spoken by the country's Bantu and Nilotic populations, respectively.",Kisankasa,Nilo-Saharan
1,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"2 weeks ago - The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Kisankasa,Nilo-Saharan
